<title>BELGIUM: FULL TEXT - CCB FIRST-HALF 1996 EARNINGS TABLE.</title>
<headline>FULL TEXT - CCB FIRST-HALF 1996 EARNINGS TABLE.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the first-half</p>
<p>1996 earnings table of Belgian publicly-owned bank Credit</p>
<p>Communal/Gemeentekrediet (CCB) as reported by the bank today.</p>
<p>CONSOLIDATED EARNINGS DATA</p>
<p>KEY FIGURES		  June 1995   June 1996  difference</p>
<p>BALANCE SHEET DATA (in billion of BEF)</p>
<p>BALANCE SHEET TOTAL	  3,332.4     3,727.4     +11.8 %</p>
<p>RESOURCES</p>
<p>Capital and reserves	    63.7	  73.8    + 15.8 %</p>
<p>Subordinated debts		44.2	  52.5    + 18.8 %</p>
<p>Credit institutions deposits 518.3	 784.8    + 51.4 %</p>
<p>Customers deposits	   2,574.6     2,665.5	+3.5 %</p>
<p> - Customers deposits	1,311.0     1,354.0     + 3.3 %</p>
<p> - Savings bonds and debentures1,263.6 1,311.5     + 3.8 %</p>
<p>ALLOCATION OF RESOURCES</p>
<p>Loans to credit institutions 600.3	 817.9     + 36.2%</p>
<p>Loans to customers	   1,393.7     1,459.8     + 4.7 %</p>
<p>Financial investments	1,192.8     1,276.7     + 7.0 %</p>
<p> - Public bonds and securities962.0	922.4     - 4.1 %</p>
<p> - Other financial assets    230.8	 354.3     +53.5 %</p>
<p>INCOME STATEMENT (millions of BEF)</p>
<p>Interest receivable	   19,663	20,673     + 5.1 %</p>
<p>Various income		   8,501	11,129    + 30.9 %</p>
<p>Total operating income	28,164	31,802    + 12.9 %</p>
<p>General expenses		16,766	17,559     + 4.7 %</p>
<p>Gross operating income	11,398	14,243    + 25.0 %</p>
<p>Depreciations, write-downs &amp; provisions</p>
<p>				     5,580	 5,250     - 5.9 %</p>
<p>Profits before tax	     5,818	 8,993    + 54.6 %</p>
<p>Profits for the period	 4,436	 6,199     +39.7 %</p>
<p> - share of minority interests 604	   787    + 30.3 %</p>
<p> - share of group		3,832	 5,412    + 41.3 %</p>
<p>On a company basis (non-consolidated)</p>
<p>Balance sheet total ( billions of BEF)</p>
<p>				     2,502	 2,756    + 10.0 %</p>
<p>Profits for the period (millions of BEF)</p>
<p>					2,978	 4,310   + 44.7 %</p>
